# Commits that touched a lot of files without changing any behavior. `git blame`
# skips them so the line it reports is the one that last said something.
#
# GitHub honors this file automatically. Locally, once per clone:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add a commit here if it is purely mechanical - a formatting sweep, a
# license-header pass, a rename. A commit that changed behavior must stay
# blameable even if it was large.

